      "content": "Thanks. I was looking at the monthly active user (MAU) numbers from the last two quarters specifically. It looks like the curve flattened out a bit compared to the initial spike. However, I know these early-stage companies often pivot their focus from raw quantity to user retention or higher LTV (lifetime value) mid-stream. \n\nIn your view, does this plateau look like a genuine stall in momentum, or could it be part of a more strategic shift in their growth model that the pitch deck didn't fully capture? I'm trying to see if the \"exponential\" story still holds weight under the surface.",
